00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.560
Episode Twenty-Four: 
Darkness Falls Again 

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.790
The Genesis Mission.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.100
Coming after the Great Mission

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.350
it is humanity's most difficult crisis.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.110
As opposed to the Great Mission, where you really couldn't feel it...

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.520
...the Genesis Mission has a real sense of urgency.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.140
We've walked on the rails built by those from long ago...

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.370
...and we were pulled along...

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.490
But this time, it's different...

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:43.850
Commander!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.360
As you were!

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:50.750
Mr. Shirogane, you're the commander of this operation, so...

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.160
Yes, sir...

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.290
What's the state of our progress?

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.700
Sir, we're on schedule for the most part.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.780
Five of the energy exposure lasers have already been deployed.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.290
They've entered their test runs.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.040
The construction of the gravity lenses that will focus the laser...

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.140
...is 90% completed.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.730
Following that, the alignment adjustment operations will begin.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.890
What about interference from the Fracture...

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.650
...when the gravity lenses are put into formation?

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.560
It's certain that Fracture's response will be proportionate to their mass...

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:30.500
...but at the same time...

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.560
...it will be inversely proportionate to the distance squared.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.310
If we can maintain that balance...

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.540
The Odyssey, the Akapusu, and the El Santo...

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.470
...are getting as close as they can to the Fracture and are standing by.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.260
The evacuation rates for the Akapusu and the Odyssey stand at 50%...

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.830
The El Santo is already 80% complete.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.230
What about both of the Gigantic Actimo Somas?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.000
The Infinity is just waiting to launch, but...

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.120
The Halcyon's adjustments are running behind...

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:11.770
Will it be ready in time?

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.880
We'll make it ready in time.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.470
Accuracy rate, 92%.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.390
Miss Katase! Miss Katase!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:15.390
Here you are.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.000
Kouta...

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.850
Are you all right?

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.440
I'm all right.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.680
I got Miss Ren to check me out, so I'm fine now.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:31.990
Shima-chan...

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:32.910
Hmm?

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.510
Trying to do something like control it without the DLS really is impossible.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.690
It's all right. For me, the DLS is a hindrance.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.200
Why are you overworking yourself so much?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.310
I'm not overworking myself or anything.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:52.340
But every day, you train until you're worn out, and just now...

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:53.180
I...!

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:58.050
All I want is to be able to do it properly.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.180
Why won't you understand?!

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:02.520
Shima-chan.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.960
Let's both do our best.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.620
Somehow, she seems kind of pitiable.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.530
Is her condition really all right?

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.470
Right now, it is.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:22.770
The fact that you trained Miss Katase this past year does show, Leila.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.860
And that's why I want to let her carry this off.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:27.910
I see.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.750
This is the third crisis for the Sol system this year.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.620
This year? Somehow it feels like a school event, doesn't it?

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.750
Yeah, it does.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.670
If we hadn't come to the Stellvia...

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.790
...we probably wouldn't have gotten to have rare experiences like this.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:51.620
But we're the ones who came here because we were meant to...

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.360
Right?

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:58.710
In that case, the Great Mission, the rescue of the Ultima...

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:04.400
...and this, the Genesis Mission, were for us, inevitable.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:10.010
Up until now, it felt like it was someone else's problem...

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.100
But this time it's a little different, you know?

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:14.820
Now then...

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.310
I'm going to go work on my machine for a bit.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.780
Open sesame. The mandolin...

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.450
Is a tremolo, it yearns for the shadow...

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.850
The two of them are young...

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:51.970
Heya.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.030
Welcome.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.260
Welcome! 
 Welcome!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.130
Were you seen by someone?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.350
I wouldn't make a blunder like that.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.470
All right!

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.970
How about joining us, sempai?

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.150
Spare me the penalty game. I'll hold off.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.410
I wanted to ask why.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.480
Why what?

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.450
Why did you brave the danger and stay behind on the Stellvia?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.550
What are you planning on doing, staying behind?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.650
Those things, I guess.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:24.360
There are various hard and soft reasons, but...

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:25.900
In any case...

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:26.700
What is it?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.910
Actually, this plan was agreed upon...

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.640
...by over one third of the preparatory and regular students.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:34.250
What?

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.310
Once we made our decision, we had to make it a reality.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.260
So, well, we had to deal with the Fujiyama's passenger register...

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.040
...balance the number of students who were evacuating and such...

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.800
We left the falsification of various things to the others...

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:47.980
...and after that was...

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.560
Just us putting it into action.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:53.560
Your advice was a big help.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.170
What a surprise.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.670
Where and how did you come up with a plan like that?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:03.720
When the outline of the Genesis Mission was announced.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.200
For the sake of humanity, for the sake of the Stellvia, 

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.200
 please meet in the basement tonight.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.200
 Be sure to come, okay?

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.450
In any case, we told the people we thought we could trust.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.260
You're quite a noble person, aren't you?

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.520
Yes, well...

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:36.970
Normally we'd include the Big Four...

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.770
...but they've already begun preparations for the Mission.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.260
I think everyone's already realized it...

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.560
...but there is a lot of uncertainty with this mission.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:46.940
And also...

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:55.960
There are quite a few unstable factors for the final mission participants.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.550
We might be able to do something about those unstable factors.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:14.980
Something, you say? Do you have a definite plan?

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:17.860
I can't say right now.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.470
No, to be blunt, I don't know what to do...

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.120
The one thing I can say...

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.510
...is that if we don't stay on the Stellvia for the Genesis Mission...

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:36.190
...with Shipon, Kouta, and the others, then we won't be able to do anything.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.310
We can't do anything as bystanders, either.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.580
In any case, please cooperate with us, everyone.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.320
I'm impressed that you convinced them with a speech like that.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.850
Wouldn't it be unfair for the adults to be the only ones...

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:51.980
...who get to make history?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:55.880
If they say they're going to use our school for a mission...

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:00.710
...we think we should at least be witnesses to that history...

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:04.850
So I guess you could say that we all at least thought that...

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:08.090
You're accomplices more than witnesses...

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.170
Oh, so am I, aren't I?

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:16.960
We're taking part in mincing logic...

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:22.280
It's no use... I can't get it right.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.690
Arisa, you still don't know where Shipon is?

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:34.520
Shh! Be quiet!

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.130
What good would it be if the old codgers in security hear you?

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:56.540
But I really don't understand the map data that jerk, Dai, gave us.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.010
Oh, this is it.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.420
The simulation room is above us.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:00.980
Oh...

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.280
Huh?

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.170
What?

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.820
What part of this is the simulation room?

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.000
That's weird...

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.910
Are you students?

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:22.360
You stayed behind?

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:23.270
Yes, sir!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:24.430
Hey!

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.270
Is this an act of rebellion?

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.580
Release of the limiters on the gravity control equipment is complete.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.520
What is the status of the evacuation of the workers?

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.850
The only ones left are the workers in the engineering department and us.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:15.780
I see. Good work.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:16.850
There's a problem!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.350
The Fracture is shifting! The energy reactions are increasing!

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:21.020
What?!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.300
One part of the Fracture is making contact!

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:37.790
It can't be! Speed up the evacuation!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.150
Another energy reaction!

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.320
Make an emergency transmission to the Stellvia!

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:52.920
Communications are down!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.740
Damn it, we've come all this way, yet...

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.010
The El Santo has been completely destroyed.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.380
Investigate the cause immediately!

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.320
Aren't things kind of bad?
 Hey, now.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.920
The El Santo has been destroyed.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.830
But the mission hasn't started, right?

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:37.640
Well then, I'll be...

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:46.740
Hurry up. Ayaka and Najima are already at the hangar.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:48.520
R-Right...

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.180
You're all to hurry to the point where the El Santo was.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:05.260
Gather as much information as you can on what happened.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.490
Roger!

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:08.970
In any case, there's a lot of things we don't know.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.270
I want each and every one of you to avoid doing anything reckless.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.830
I think going right up to the Fracture is reckless from the start, though...

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:18.740
Don't say that, don't say that.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:20.730
Sorry to keep you waiting.
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:21.940
You're late. 
You're late.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:35.990
The mission is going to begin in an hour?!

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.230
Perhaps that's a little too unreasonable?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:40.730
Seriously!

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:42.700
I know it's unreasonable.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.180
This is the data that was sent to us just a short time ago...

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.110
...from the Katie formation that went ahead.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.200
There's an increase in the activities of the Fracture.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:56.930
If we don't start the mission right now, the Odyssey and the Akapusu...

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.610
...and our very own Stellvia will meet the same fate as the El Santo.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:04.050
But neither Katase's training nor the Halcyon's adjustments...

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:05.260
...have been finished.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.240
Her accuracy has surpassed 90%, right?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.460
But...

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.990
And the Halcyon's cockpit's modifications are finished, right?

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.960
That is certainly true, but there hasn't been enough testing.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:19.950
And there still remains the work to swap out the propulsion systems.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.440
Let's give up on increasing mobility.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:27.240
We'll have to have Miss Katase do the final adjustments after launch.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:28.450
All right?

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:31.250
I understand.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:35.150
Katase, I think you understand, too, but under the circumstances...

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.220
...we have no choice but to send out the Halcyon in inadequate condition.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.490
Despite that, will you do this for us?

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:42.710
Yes, sir!

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.900
Shima-chan, I...

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:08.880
What is it?

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:13.560
I... That's why... Shima-chan, I...

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:15.460
It's all right.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.290
Even if the units we're piloting are separate, it's all right.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.160
Let's do our best, Kouta.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.440
Shima-chan?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:29.760
Four... three... two... one...

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.740
Start the Genesis Mission!

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.210
Starting the mission.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.640
Laser cannon wheels are rotating.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.530
Tatsuonoff generators activated.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.050
Beginning activation of the gravity lens system.

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:08.360
Gravity catapult preparations okay.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.220
Launching the Infinity!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:15.720
Please move the Halcyon to the catapult.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:16.720
Roger.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:30.770
Why? Why aren't there any generators attached to Rukyon?

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:32.270
Rukyon?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.130
I decided that just now!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:37.600
That's right, that's right! Attach them to Rukyon, too!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.280
But these are still being adjusted.

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:40.980
What? 
What?

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:46.650
Originally, this was supposed to have been more than ready...

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:47.620
...by the time the mission began.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:50.320
But...

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.550
That can't be... 
That can't be...

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.230
Katase, I don't want to sound like a cliche. So I'll just say good luck.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:01.160
If this goes well, I'll give you an "A" in any course you choose.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:02.120
Yes, sir.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.460
Launching the Halcyon.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:20.570
How much longer until they're finished?

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.680
A little less than two hours maybe?

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:25.160
That's a waste!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.630
In that case, then at least...

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:27.660
Hmm?

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.240
In that case, then I want to at least...

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.640
...get the adjustments finished, and deliver them to her...

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.080
There isn't only one shot, is there?

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:36.830
It's fine, even if it's just barely enough.

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:38.200
I want to get those to Shipon...

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:39.800
We'll take part in that, too!

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.250
Where in the world are we going?

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.510
It looks like Arisa and the others found something to do...

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.350
...so we're going to go and do what we can do.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.550
We've been through here before, haven't we?

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:00.880
Yeah, it couldn't be, it just might be...

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.700
We're going to climb up?!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:06.570
Yeah.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.720
The generators are beginning preparations for launch.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:10.760
What?!

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.690
Three preparatory students' Biancas are being prepared as well.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:15.470
Biancas?!

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:20.480
Those guys! When in the world...?!

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:31.490
Go!

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:44.830
Whoa, they're fast!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:46.670
Come on, let's hurry.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.860
Fujisawa, Kazamatsuri, Takida, come back!

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.890
Please let them go.

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:56.660
Professor Turner.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.780
It is better for the sake of the future.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.610
Yahoo!

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:28.640
So we're here, after all.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:50.760
I just have to do what I can to the best of my abilities.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:54.230
Mother... Arisa... Kouta...

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:07.530
Next Episode 

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:06.840
This is Shima. 

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:07.730
This is Ayaka Machida.

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:09.470
The Genesis Mission is starting, isn't it?

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:12.480
It's fine that it's starting, but what are you going to do about Otoyama?

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:14.180
Um, well, that is...

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:16.890
If the two of you don't get along, you'll just hinder the mission.

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:17.620
Right...

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:20.150
If that happens, as your sempai, what should I do?

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:21.900
Give advice? A suggestion?

00:23:21.990 --> 00:23:23.410
That might end up being the chance for me...

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:24.720
...to start a relationship with a younger boy, and...

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:26.930
Oh, what am I saying?

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:29.450
And thus, on the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.240
"Goodbye." Don't miss it.

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:32.810
What? It's "Goodbye"?

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:35.550
Episode Twenty-Five:
 Goodbye 

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:34.730
Please look forward to it! "Goodbye."
